From: Yusuf İhsan KILINÇ <78423442+yusufklncc@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 15:20:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 13] anv: index the mutable descriptor type lists by pBindings
 index, not binding number

VkMutableDescriptorTypeCreateInfoEXT::pMutableDescriptorTypeLists[i]
describes pBindings[i] of the VkDescriptorSetLayoutCreateInfo it chains
to (radv and nvk index it so, and so does anv's own
GetDescriptorSetLayoutSupport). anv_CreateDescriptorSetLayout walks the
bindings sorted by binding number and looked the list up with that
number b instead of the pBindings index (info_idx). With sparse or
unordered binding numbers a mutable binding got another binding's list,
or none when b >= mutableDescriptorTypeListCount, which sizes it for
every descriptor type: a sampler state in the sampler heap and the
largest surface size.

Seen with a layout whose mutable storage-image band sits at binding
numbers 480-607 with 321 lists: every set took 160 sampler states instead
of 32, so a descriptor pool sized from the same lists (which pools index
correctly, by pPoolSizes index) held a fifth of its maxSets
(VK_ERROR_OUT_OF_POOL_MEMORY at 51 of 256 sets).

